        <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 list-disc pl-5">
          <li><strong>Fixing PDF and OCR Extractions:</strong> When copying content out of multi-column PDF layouts or scanned Google Books, paragraph breaks frequently arrive with erratic double or triple blank lines. Collapsing consecutive blank lines restores natural reading cadence.</li>
          <li><strong>Source Code and SQL Formatting:</strong> Minified JavaScript code, pasted SQL queries, or configuration YAML files frequently accumulate accidental empty line gaps that clutter visual screen real estate.</li>
          <li><strong>Markdown Documentation Hygiene:</strong> Markdown engines rely on precise line breaks for headers, blockquotes, and lists. Standardizing line gaps prevents irregular rendering in static site generators like Astro or Jekyll.</li>
          <li><strong>Database and CSV Prep:</strong> Spreadsheet exports from Excel or Google Sheets often include trailing blank rows that cause import syntax errors during database migration scripts.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ Section (SEO crawlable) -->
  <section class="py-16 sm:py-24">
